  "scope": [
    "Bound native file backing and UTF-16 decoding admission from the actual verified descriptor before Buffer.alloc, using the existing fixed 512 MiB Node allowance.",
    "Preparse scan counts primitive slots, array/object storage, key storage and UTF-16 strings without token arrays/decoded keys; rejects excessive tree capacity or nesting before JSON.parse. Whitespace is charged to text storage but does not inflate the decoded tree estimate.",
    "One ingestion ledger admits eight conservative tree copies while parsing and keeps four capacities for preceding native assets. Backings from completed descriptor reads retire by native detachment; failed input reservations release. All original checksum, version/schema, resource verification and descriptor rules remain.",
    "The unchanged Node allowance now belongs to the shared scene contract, preserving the runtime re-export and worker partition. Original private cross-package import was rejected and fixed through the public contract."
  ],
  "qualification": "This is an ingestion-stage foundation, not complete aggregate source/preparation/export admission. The sourceAdmission receipt is captured before catalogue/variant preparation and handed to callers as evidence; the ingestion ledger closes at that boundary. It does not claim to admit retained prepared variants, whole source/result RPC coexistence, world/body/replay, driver internals or process RSS. Original file 32 MiB, binary 32 MiB, Node 512 MiB and replay quotas remain fixed. No complete MS2 gate, installed refresh or human acceptance is claimed.",
